      en: "The Byblos coast stretches 8 km along the Mediterranean, featuring a mix of sandy beaches and rocky shores. The ancient harbor, continuously used for over 5,000 years, is a key archaeological site. The coastal zone supports a small fishery with annual catches around 300 tons. Water quality is generally good, but urban runoff has caused localized pollution. Byblos receives about 600,000 visitors annually, making it one of Lebanon's top tourist destinations. The coast is also a nesting site for green turtles.",
